# 3. CGP program

<div class="code-path">Code: <code>examples/c1-cgp-template/</code>, <code>scripts/build_examples.py</code></div>

A program written with a library works in the same way, as long as the library can be compiled for the web.
The objective of this example is to show it with [CGP](https://github.com/drohmer/cgp-2027), a C++ library
made for teaching computer graphics: we take the template project of CGP, and compile it for the web without
changing a line.

Once built, you should observe the following scene: the mouse rotates the camera, the ImGui window of the
template stays on screen, and the arrow keys still go to the next slide.

